/* Civicsmith mockups: the 46 screens of the registry (registry.src.py), each a function of the context
   c = {ai: the member has connected their own Claude account, v: a variant name}. Sample data is invented:
   the team Lakeshore Tenants, its members Rosa (founder), Dev, Mai (new), Ana (an accountant) and Teo (a reporter). */
'use strict';
const G = { name: 'Lakeshore Tenants', slug: 'lakeshore-tenants', me: 'Mai' };
const SCR = {};
// DEC-180 (Bob, S17, K2108): one reminder wherever a member takes or adds a photo
const PHOTO_REMINDER = '<p class="mk-small muted" style="margin:0">Frame what you are checking, and leave out people\'s faces and number plates where you can. If a published case carries this photo, anyone in it who is not part of a finding, and any number plate, is obscured in the public copy; the original stays inside your team.</p>';

/* DEC-374 (B398 C11; instance-setup groupdomainset): the one small file a team puts on its website to prove its address, shown
   where the address is typed: the file offered, where it goes and at what address, the check, and what its refusals say. */
const domainFile = () => `<details class="mk-details"><summary>The file for your website</summary>
  <p class="mk-small">Put this one small file on your website. Once it is there, anyone reading what your team publishes can check that it comes from you. It holds nothing secret: only your team's Civicsmith address and short name.</p>
  <div class="cs-sheet" style="padding:10px 14px;display:grid;gap:6px"><b class="mk-small">civicsmith-group.json</b><pre class="mk-small mk-data" style="margin:0;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere">{ "instance": "https://lakeshore-tenants.rosa-m.workers.dev", "group": "lakeshore-tenants" }</pre><div class="mk-acts"><a href="#" onclick="return false" class="cs-btn" data-tone="primary">Download the file</a></div></div>
  <p class="mk-small"><b>What to do with it</b>, or hand this to whoever looks after your website:</p>
  <ol class="mk-small" style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;display:grid;gap:4px">
   <li>Save the file without changing its name or what is inside it.</li>
   <li>On your website, make a folder named <span class="mk-data">.well-known</span>, with the dot at the start, at the very top of the site, beside the home page. Some website builders hide this step: ask their support to add it.</li>
   <li>Put the file in that folder.</li>
   <li>Open <span class="mk-data">https://lakeshoretenants.org/.well-known/civicsmith-group.json</span> in a browser. It must show the file's text at once, without signing in and without sending you to another page.</li>
   <li>Come back here and ask Civicsmith to check it, with the button above.</li></ol>
  <p class="mk-small">Civicsmith reads the file as soon as you ask for the check, and again once a day, so a website that later drops the file stops being shown as verified.</p>
  <details class="mk-details"><summary>When the check does not pass</summary><div style="display:grid;gap:6px">
   ${gapm('refused', 'That is not a website name. Type only the name, such as example-tenants.org: no https://, no page, no port and no numbers-only address. Nothing was recorded.')}
   ${gapm('refused', 'Civicsmith found no file at that address, or the website sent it to another page. Check the folder name and the file name, and that the file opens without signing in, then ask for the check again.')}
   ${gapm('refused', 'The file there is not this one. It names a different Civicsmith address or short name than your team\'s, or it is not the kind of file Civicsmith reads. Replace it with the file from this page, then ask for the check again.')}
   ${gapm('undetermined', 'Civicsmith could not reach the website just now. This says nothing against it, and your team is not marked as failing. Try again in a few minutes.')}
   ${gapm('refused', 'Only an administrator can verify the website. Ask one of your team\'s administrators to do it.')}</div></details></details>`;

/* DEC-374 (B398 C9; promotion reopen): reopening a finding that a published case carries, with a reason; the way to a correction. */
const reopenFinding = () => `<details class="mk-details"><summary>Reopen this finding, with a reason</summary>
  <p class="mk-small">Reopening takes the conclusion off this question, so the team can work on it again. The published case that carries it stays exactly as it was published until a next edition replaces it. Your name and your reason are kept in the question's history.</p>
  ${field('mk-reopenwhy', 'Why it no longer holds', '', { reason: true, act: 'reopen', help: 'Required. One line of at most 160 characters, with no quotation marks or backslashes, such as: the city\'s 2026 audit corrects the figure.' })}
  ${acts(btn('reopen', 'Reopen this finding'))}
  <p class="mk-small">Next, correct the question and conclude it again. Then you can ${ref('start the next edition of the case', 'docket', '<b>Docket</b> · after publishing: each correction, withdrawal and court order on a published case, and where the next edition is started.')}.</p>
  <details class="mk-details"><summary>When the reopening is refused</summary><div style="display:grid;gap:6px">
   ${gapm('refused', 'Say why first: a finding is reopened only with a reason, and it stays concluded until you give one.')}
   ${gapm('refused', 'That reason cannot be kept as written. Use one line of at most 160 characters, with no quotation marks or backslashes.')}
   ${gapm('refused', 'This finding is concluded and is in no published case, so it cannot be reopened. Withdraw its conclusion instead, with a reason.')}</div></details></details>`;

/* ---------------- the team's Civicsmith: installing, setting up, joining ---------------- */
/* DEC-201 (B158, B159; K3052, K3053): the way in. The front door with sign-in, a forgotten password, the installer as a
   sequence from the founder's link to the hand-over, team settings, the Projects list, the Settings index, the outside
   reviewer's view, the update page and the screens for an address that can't be opened. Where Bob's questions on BOB's
   review page are still open (the front door, a member's lost password, how long a sign-in lasts, the free plan, where
   the founder's link lives), the screens follow the recommendation and DEC-201 names each such part. */
const FRONT_ST = { signin: 'a', refused: 'b', paused: 'c', signedout: 'd', ended: 'e', locked: 'f' };
SCR.front = c => { const st = FRONT_ST[c.v] || 'a'; const sel = v => v === st ? ' selected' : ''; return { frame: 'public', title: 'Lakeshore Tenants', st, main: `
  <div class="mk-mockctl"><label for="mk-fst">In this mockup, show the team's page</label> <select id="mk-fst" class="cs-input" onchange="this.closest('main').dataset.st=this.value"><option value="a"${sel('a')}>to a visitor</option><option value="b"${sel('b')}>after a refused sign-in</option><option value="c"${sel('c')}>while sign-in is paused</option><option value="d"${sel('d')}>just after signing out</option><option value="e"${sel('e')}>after a sign-in ended for being idle</option><option value="f"${sel('f')}>locked, on a device kept signed in</option></select></div>
  <div class="mk-front">
   <header class="mk-fronthead"><div class="mk-flogo" aria-hidden="true">LT</div><div><span class="grp mk-grp">Lakeshore Tenants</span><p class="mk-sub mk-data">Tenants near the Oakland Coliseum, checking whether the city keeps its own rules and promises: on rents and leases on city land, and the streets we live on. Meeting since 2025.</p></div></header>
   <div class="st st-f">${sec('Welcome back, Mai', `${row(I('hold'), '<b>Locked after 30 minutes away.</b> Enter your password to go on where you were; nothing was lost.', '')}${field('mk-lkp', 'Password', '', { act: 'unlock' })}${acts(btn('unlock', 'Unlock', { tone: 'primary' }), link('Not Mai? Sign in as someone else'))}`)}</div>
   <div class="mk-frontgrid st st-a st-b st-c st-d st-e">
    <div>
     ${sec('What we have published', sheet(row(I('case'), '<b>The Coliseum lease</b><span class="meta">Edition 2 · September 18, 2026 · signed by Dev</span><span class="mk-small mk-data">The city collected rent under a lease amendment its council never voted on.</span>', '') + row(I('case'), '<b class="mk-data">Pothole repairs on our streets</b><span class="meta">Edition 1 · October 2, 2026 · signed by Mai</span><span class="mk-small mk-data">Of the reports the city marked closed within seven days, about four in five were repaired.</span>', '')) + `<div class="mk-acts">${ref('All our published cases', 'published', '<b>Published cases</b> · the team\'s signed, public work, which anyone may read and check')}</div>`)}
     ${sec('Have something for us?', `${note('Documents, photos or a tip: you can hand them to the team without an account. Nobody is told who you are unless you say.')}<div class="mk-acts">${ref(I('add') + 'Hand material to the team', 'doorbell', '<b>Hand material to the team</b> · send documents or a tip without an account')}</div>`)}
     ${sec('How we work', `${note('We use Civicsmith, free software for checking public records: every finding cites its source, says how strong the evidence is, and is signed by a member.')}<div class="mk-acts">${ref(I('wizard') + 'See how it works, step by step', 'tour', '<b>The guided walk-through</b> · how a team like ours works, for anyone: before joining, invited, or a member')}</div>`)}
    </div>
    <div class="mk-signin">
     ${sec('Members', `<div class="st st-d">${row(I('accepted'), '<b>You are signed out on this device.</b> Your work is saved in your team\'s Civicsmith, not here.', '')}</div><div class="st st-e">${row(I('clock'), '<b>You were signed out after a while away</b>, so nobody else at this device can use your sign-in. Sign in again to go back to the page you were on.', '')}</div>
      ${field('mk-sih', 'Your handle', 'mai-k', { act: 'login', help: 'The name the team knows you by: chosen when you joined, or when you set the team up.' })}
      ${field('mk-sip', 'Password', '••••••••••••••', { act: 'login' })}
      ${checks('This device is', [['My own: keep me signed in (it locks after 30 minutes away; you sign in again after 12 hours)', true], ['Shared or public: sign me out after 15 minutes away', false]], { radio: true, act: 'login' })}
      <div class="st st-b"><div class="cs-gap" data-gap="refused">${I('refused')}<span>That handle and password don't match. Check both and try again; after several tries, sign-in pauses for a while to keep others from guessing.</span></div></div>
      <div class="st st-c"><div class="cs-gap" data-gap="refused">${I('refused')}<span>Sign-in is paused for a while after too many tries from here. This keeps others from guessing passwords; it isn't a judgment on you. Try again at 10:42 AM.</span></div></div>
      ${acts(btn('login', 'Sign in', { tone: 'primary' }), ref('Forgot your password?', 'forgot', '<b>Forgot your password?</b> · how a member gets back in'))}
      <p class="mk-small">Invited? Open the link you were sent: it brings you here to join.</p>`)}
    </div>
   </div>
  </div>
  <p class="mk-small muted">Lakeshore Tenants uses Civicsmith.</p>` }; };

const FORGOT_ST = { choose: 'a', done: 'b', refused: 'c' };
/* DEC-205 (BOB's B162 (5); Bob's D7, K3060): the walk-through for anyone, from the team's page, with no account. Six short
   steps, each one screen; Back and Next move between them, and "Stop here" returns to the team's page at any step. */
const TOUR = [
  ['What we look into', `<p>Lakeshore Tenants looks into <span class="mk-data">rents and leases on city land, and the streets we live on</span>. We check what the city says against its own records, and publish what the records show.</p>`],
  ['Every finding shows its source', `<p>Each finding we publish points to the passage it rests on: a page of a budget, a line of the minutes, a row of an office's own data. Open any finding in a published case and the passage opens with it, so you can read it yourself.</p>`],
  ['How strong the evidence is', `<p>Each piece of evidence carries a letter, A strongest to D weakest, and says why it has that letter: a copy fetched from the office's own website holds up better than one found elsewhere. A finding is never stronger than its weakest piece, and where something isn't known, the case says so instead of guessing.</p>`],
  ['What we publish, and who stands behind it', `<p>A case is published only when a member signs it. Once published it is never changed quietly: a correction comes as a new edition, and the earlier one stays readable with the correction beside it.</p>`],
  ['Have something for us?', `<p>Anyone can hand us documents or a tip without an account. The page says what will happen to what you give, and you decide how much to tell us about yourself.</p>`],
  ['Taking part', `<p>Members join by an invitation from one of our administrators. If you would like to take part, ask a member you know, or tell us through “Have something for us?”. Members sign in from our page.</p>`]];
const TOUR_ST = ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e', 'f'];
SCR.tour = c => { const st = TOUR_ST.includes(c.v) ? c.v : 'a'; const sel = v => v === st ? ' selected' : ''; const go = k => `this.closest('main').dataset.st='${k}';var s=this.closest('main').querySelector('#mk-tst');if(s)s.value='${k}'`;
  return { frame: 'public', title: 'How we work, step by step', st, main: `
  <div class="mk-mockctl"><label for="mk-tst">In this mockup, show</label> <select id="mk-tst" class="cs-input" onchange="this.closest('main').dataset.st=this.value">${TOUR.map((t, i) => `<option value="${TOUR_ST[i]}"${sel(TOUR_ST[i])}>step ${i + 1}: ${t[0]}</option>`).join('')}</select></div>
  <div class="mk-setuphead"><span class="grp mk-grp">Lakeshore Tenants</span></div>
  ${TOUR.map(([t, body], i) => `<div class="st st-${TOUR_ST[i]}"><div class="cs-wizard"><span class="step">${I('wizard')} Step ${i + 1} of ${TOUR.length} · how we work</span><span class="what">${t}</span>${body}
   <div class="nav">${i > 0 ? `<button type="button" class="cs-btn" onclick="${go(TOUR_ST[i - 1])}">Back</button>` : ''}${i < TOUR.length - 1 ? `<button type="button" class="cs-btn" data-tone="primary" onclick="${go(TOUR_ST[i + 1])}">Next</button>` : ''}${ref(i === TOUR.length - 1 ? 'Back to our page' : 'Stop here', 'front', '<b>Your team&#39;s page</b> · Lakeshore Tenants&#39; own page, where this walk-through started')}</div></div>
   ${i === 4 ? acts(ref(I('add') + 'Have something for us?', 'doorbell', '<b>Have something for us?</b> · hand the team documents or a tip, with no account')) : ''}</div>`).join('')}
  ${note('No account is needed and nothing you do here is recorded. Members see the same walk-through from Home.')}` }; };

/* DEC-205 (BOB's B162 (5); Bob's D4, K3060): an administrator's one-time reset link opens here. */
const RESET_ST = { done: 'b', dead: 'c' };
SCR.reset = c => { const st = RESET_ST[c.v] || 'a'; const sel = v => v === st ? ' selected' : ''; return { frame: 'public', title: 'Choose a new password', st, main: `
  <div class="mk-mockctl"><label for="mk-rst">In this mockup, show</label> <select id="mk-rst" class="cs-input" onchange="this.closest('main').dataset.st=this.value"><option value="a"${sel('a')}>the reset link opened</option><option value="b"${sel('b')}>the new password set</option><option value="c"${sel('c')}>a link that no longer works</option></select></div>
  <div class="mk-setuphead"><span class="grp mk-grp">Lakeshore Tenants</span></div>
  <div class="st st-a">${h1('Choose a new password', 'For mai-k · a reset link Rosa made on October 12 · it works once, until October 19')}<div style="display:grid;gap:16px;margin-top:16px">
   ${field('mk-np', 'A new password', '', { act: 'passwordreset', help: 'At least 12 characters.' })}${field('mk-np2', 'Type it again', '', { act: 'passwordreset' })}
   ${acts(btn('passwordreset', 'Set my new password', { tone: 'primary' }))}
   ${note('Your handle and everything you did stay as they are, and every other sign-in of yours ends. Rosa can\'t see the password you choose. Your recovery codes still work; if you have lost them too, get ten new ones in Settings › Recovery codes once you are in.')}</div></div>
  <div class="st st-b">${h1('Choose a new password', 'For mai-k')}${row(I('accepted'), '<b>Your new password is set.</b> The reset link is spent, and every other sign-in of yours has ended. Sign in with your new password.', '')}${acts(ref('Sign in', 'front', '<b>Sign in</b> · your team&#39;s page, where members sign in'))}</div>
  <div class="st st-c">${h1('This link no longer works', 'A reset link works once, for seven days')}${row(I('refused'), 'It was used already, it expired, or an administrator withdrew it. Ask an administrator for a new one, in person or however your team talks. Nothing was changed.', '')}${acts(ref('Back to your team\'s page', 'front', '<b>Your team&#39;s page</b> · where members sign in'))}</div>` }; };

SCR.forgot = c => { const st = FORGOT_ST[c.v] || 'a'; const sel = v => v === st ? ' selected' : ''; return { frame: 'public', title: 'Forgot your password', st, main: `
  <div class="mk-mockctl"><label for="mk-gst">In this mockup, show</label> <select id="mk-gst" class="cs-input" onchange="this.closest('main').dataset.st=this.value"><option value="a"${sel('a')}>the two ways back in</option><option value="b"${sel('b')}>a new password set with a recovery code</option><option value="c"${sel('c')}>a recovery code that didn't work</option></select></div>
  <div class="mk-setuphead"><span class="grp mk-grp">Lakeshore Tenants</span></div>
  ${h1('Forgot your password', 'Civicsmith sends no email, so getting back in goes through your team, not a mailbox.')}
  <div class="st st-b">${row(I('accepted'), '<b>Your new password is set.</b> That recovery code is spent; you have 7 left. Every other sign-in of yours has ended. Sign in with your new password.', '')}${acts(ref('Sign in', 'front', '<b>Sign in</b> · the front door'))}</div>
  <div class="st st-a st-c">${sec('Use one of your recovery codes', `${field('mk-rh', 'Your handle', 'rosa', { act: 'recover', help: 'The handle you sign in with: the name the team knows you by.' })}${field('mk-rc', 'One of your recovery codes', '7KQ2-M4XD-P9TR', { act: 'recover', help: 'One of the ten codes you saved when you joined, or got later in Settings › Recovery codes. Each works once.' })}${field('mk-rp', 'A new password', '', { act: 'recover', help: 'At least 12 characters.' })}${field('mk-rp2', 'Type it again', '', { act: 'recover' })}
   <div class="st st-c"><div class="cs-gap" data-gap="refused">${I('refused')}<span>That didn't work: the handle, the code or both aren't right, or the code was already used. Check them and try again. Nothing was changed.</span></div></div>
   ${acts(btn('recover', 'Set my new password', { tone: 'primary' }))}`)}
   ${sec('No codes to hand? Ask an administrator', `${note('An administrator can make you a reset link, like an invitation: it works once, for seven days, and lets you choose a new password. Ask an administrator in person or however your team talks. No administrator can see your password, and you keep your handle and everything you did.')}`)}
   ${sec('If no administrator can get in', note('Whoever holds your team\'s Cloudflare account can set a new one-time password and an administrator can claim again from it. That is the way back in when every administrator has lost both their password and their codes.'))}</div>` }; };

const INSTALL_ST = { start: 'a', cloudflare: 'b', progress: 'c', refused: 'd', done: 'e', nosite: 'f', existing: 'g', remove: 'h', ready: 'i', check: 'j', checkok: 'k', step1: 'l', step2: 'm', step3: 'n', account: 'o', address: 'p', guide4: 'q', stop: 'r' };
/* DEC-416 (beneath Bob's DEC-415): "Get ready", a guide ahead of the installer, and "Check my account", the gate. Every button of the guide opens Cloudflare's own page in a new tab (an outside link, marked as sample data: the exact addresses are checked on a schedule, installer R70's guide check). */
const CF = (href, label) => `<span class="mk-data"><a class="cs-btn" data-tone="quiet" href="${href}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${I('outward')}${esc(label)}</a></span>`;
/* DEC-206 (Bob's D6, K3060: "The founding journey should now start on the website we need to develop at civicsmith.org").
   civicsmith.org is Civicsmith's own site, kept by its stewards: what Civicsmith is (installer R42's two lines, exactly), a case a
   team published, the teams that chose to be listed (DEC-132), and "Start your team", which says what a team needs before the
   installer asks anything. It holds no accounts: members sign in at their own team's address. The installer's first page then
   asks only its two choices, so nothing is explained twice. */
const SITE_ST = { home: 'a', start: 'b', groups: 'c', none: 'd' };
/* DEC-206 (Bob's D6), rewritten under DEC-223 (Bob, October 14): civicsmith.org is one website of three pages, joined by one
   menu on every page: the front page, for someone who has never heard of Civicsmith; "Start a team", for a member who has
   decided to create their team's copy; "Teams at work", the teams that chose to be listed. Each page is written for its
   reader: the front page defines every word before it uses it; the start page says what is needed, who holds what, what
   happens step by step, and what it costs. */
const SITE_LINE1 = 'Civicsmith is free software for a team of people who want to know whether their government is doing what it must: obeying the laws that bind it and the court decisions it is subject to, keeping the rules it set for itself and the promises it made.';
const SITE_LINE2 = 'The team gathers the records, works out what they show, and publishes what it finds in a form anyone can check. Neighborhood groups, newsrooms, professional associations and offices checking their own work all use it the same way.';
SCR.site = c => { const st = SITE_ST[c.v] || 'a'; const sel = v => v === st ? ' selected' : ''; const go = k => `this.closest('main').dataset.st='${k}';return false`;
  const nav = cur => `<nav class="mk-sitenav" aria-label="civicsmith.org">${[['a', 'What Civicsmith is'], ['b', 'Start a team'], ['c', 'Teams at work']].map(([k, t]) => `<a href="#"${k === cur ? ' aria-current="page"' : ''} onclick="${go(k)}" data-tip="${k === cur ? `<b>${t}</b>: the page you are on.` : `<b>${t}</b>: ${k === 'a' ? 'the front page of civicsmith.org: what Civicsmith is and how a team uses it' : k === 'b' ? 'for a team that has decided to create its own copy: what it needs, who holds what, what happens step by step, and what it costs' : 'the teams that chose to be listed, with what each has published'}.<span class=more>Press or tap to open it.</span>`}">${t}</a>`).join('')}</nav>`;
  return { frame: 'setup', title: 'civicsmith.org', st, main: `
  <div class="mk-mockctl"><label for="mk-sst">In this mockup, show the page of civicsmith.org</label> <select id="mk-sst" class="cs-input" onchange="this.closest('main').dataset.st=this.value"><option value="a"${sel('a')}>the front page: what Civicsmith is</option><option value="b"${sel('b')}>Start a team</option><option value="c"${sel('c')}>Teams at work</option><option value="d"${sel('d')}>Teams at work, before any team is listed</option></select></div>
  <div class="mk-setuphead"><svg viewBox="0 0 60 90" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-mark"/></svg><span class="mk-wordmark">Civicsmith</span><span class="muted">civicsmith.org</span></div>
  <div class="st st-a">${nav('a')}${h1('Hold your government to its own word', SITE_LINE1 + ' ' + SITE_LINE2)}
   ${acts(`<a href="#" class="cs-btn" data-tone="primary" onclick="${go('b')}">Start a team's Civicsmith</a>`, `<a href="#" class="cs-btn" onclick="${go('c')}">See what teams have published</a>`)}
   ${sec('How a team uses it', `<ol class="mk-list"><li><b>Gather the records.</b> Members collect the records that bear on the question, from wherever they were published: the city's minutes, budgets, contracts and letters; state and federal regulations and reports; court decisions; the press releases and filings of private firms. Civicsmith keeps each one exactly as its source published it, with where and when it came from. Together these are the team's <b>record</b>.</li><li><b>Ask a question.</b> In the team's own words: “Did the city collect the rent its lease requires?”</li><li><b>Weigh the evidence.</b> Members mark the passages of the record that bear on the question. Civicsmith grades each passage by how easily a stranger could check it, from a copy fetched straight from the office down to one person's word.</li><li><b>Reach a finding.</b> The team's answer to its question, resting on named evidence, with how strong that evidence is. A hunch is kept as a hunch; it never becomes a finding.</li><li><b>Publish a case.</b> The findings, their evidence and their strength, published together and signed by a member of the team. Anyone can read it and check it without asking the team.</li></ol>`)}
   ${sec('What a team gets', `<ul class="mk-list"><li><b>Its own copy of Civicsmith.</b> Each team runs its own copy, in a Cloudflare account the team controls. Nobody else holds the team's work, the people who make Civicsmith included.</li><li><b>Findings anyone can check.</b> Every finding points to the passages it rests on and says how strong that evidence is, so a reader never has to take the team's word for it.</li><li><b>Help for people who have never done this.</b> A guide walks each common job step by step, from asking an office for a record to publishing a case. An AI assistant is optional: it answers only from what the team holds, says where it looked, and never concludes, signs or sends. Everything works without it.</li><li><b>Free software.</b> Civicsmith costs nothing. The team pays Cloudflare $5 a month for the account its copy runs in.</li></ul>`)}
   ${sec('What Civicsmith does not do', `<ul class="mk-list"><li>It takes no side on what policy should be. It asks only whether the government kept its word.</li><li>It gives legal information, never legal advice.</li><li>It publishes nothing a member has not signed, and it sends no email.</li></ul>`)}
   ${sec('One team\'s work', `${row(I('case'), `<b>${ref('The Coliseum lease, Edition 2', 'published', '<b>Edition 2</b> of The Coliseum lease · a case Lakeshore Tenants published on September 18, 2026, at the time Dev set when signing<span class=more>Click to open it as any reader sees it.</span>', 'mk-data')}</b><span class="meta">Lakeshore Tenants, Oakland · signed by Dev · <span class="mk-data">whether the city kept the terms of its lease of the Coliseum land</span></span>`, '')}${note('Open it as any reader does: each finding, its evidence and how strong it is, and a way to check the signature without asking the team.')}`)}
   ${sec('Already a member of a team?', note('Your team\'s Civicsmith has its own address, and you sign in there, not here: civicsmith.org holds no accounts. Ask your team for its address, or find it on your team\'s own website.'))}
   ${sec('Questions', note('Write to the people who make Civicsmith: <b>[the stewards\' address, set up with civicsmith.org\'s email]</b>.'))}</div>
  <div class="st st-b">${nav('b')}${h1('Start a team\'s Civicsmith', 'For a team that has decided to create its own copy. This page says what you need, who should hold what, what happens step by step, and what it costs. Reading it takes five minutes; the installer takes about twenty.')}
   ${sec('Is it right for your team?', `<p>It fits if your team wants to find out whether a government, agency or public body is keeping the laws, rules and promises that bind it, and to show what the records say in a way others can check. It does not fit a team that wants a place to post opinions, or one that needs a lawyer's advice: Civicsmith gives neither.</p>`)}
   ${sec('What you need', `<ul class="mk-list"><li><b>A Cloudflare account on the Workers Paid plan</b>, $5 a month, with a payment method. Cloudflare is the company whose computers will run your team's copy. Open the account in your team's name, not a person's.</li><li><b>About twenty minutes</b> at a computer.</li><li><b>Nothing else.</b> No server, no company, no technical knowledge, and no Claude account: the assistant is optional, and members connect their own accounts later if they want it. The installer asks you two things and does the rest.</li><li>No Cloudflare account yet? The installer walks you through opening one, step by step.</li></ul>`)}
   ${sec('Decide first: who holds the Cloudflare account', note('Whoever can sign in to that account controls your team\'s Civicsmith. They can read everything in it, and they are the way back in if every administrator is ever locked out. Agree as a team on who that is, and add a second trusted person to the account, so it never depends on one person. The installer says this again at the moment it matters.'))}
   ${sec('What happens, step by step', `<ol class="mk-list"><li><b>You choose a short name and your places.</b> The short name is a fixed label in your team's addresses and beside every signature; it never changes. The places are the city, county and state whose rules apply to you. Places ready now: Oakland, Alameda County and California. For each, Civicsmith already holds the local facts it works from: its offices, where its records are published, its deadlines and its holidays.</li><li><b>Cloudflare asks your permission</b>, on its own page, to let the installer create your team's copy in your account.</li><li><b>The installer puts your team's Civicsmith in place and checks it.</b> About ten minutes. If a step stops, the installer says why and what to do; a stop before setup has begun creates nothing.</li><li><b>You claim it.</b> The installer shows you a one-time password; you use it once, choose your own password, and become the team's first administrator. More administrators can be added later.</li><li><b>You set it up.</b> Your team's name, the languages its members use, and whether members may use the assistant. All of it can be changed later.</li><li><b>You invite members.</b> Each gets a link you send yourself, by whatever means you trust; Civicsmith sends no email. Each member chooses the name their work will carry.</li></ol>`)}
   ${sec('What it costs', note('$5 a month to Cloudflare for the account. If members use the assistant, its use is paid to Anthropic by whoever connected the account that serves it, and the team can set limits. Nothing is paid to the people who make Civicsmith.'))}
   ${acts(ref(I('wizard') + 'Create your team', 'install', '<b>The installer</b> · asks your short name and places, then takes you to Cloudflare to allow it'), `<a href="#" class="cs-btn" onclick="${go('a')}">Back to the front page</a>`)}</div>
  <div class="st st-c">${nav('c')}${h1('Teams at work', 'The teams that chose to be listed here, each with what it has published. A team may keep itself to its members; then it is not listed, and nothing on this page is asked of it.')}
   ${sheet(row(I('group'), `<b>Lakeshore Tenants</b> · Oakland, California<span class="meta"><span class="mk-data">Rents and leases on city land, and the streets we live on</span> · 1 published case, in 2 editions, the latest September 18</span>`, ref('Visit', 'front', '<b>Lakeshore Tenants\' page</b> · its own page, at its own address: what it has published and how to hand it material')) + row(I('group'), `<b>West Oakland Neighbors</b> · Oakland, California<span class="meta"><span class="mk-data">Illegal dumping and how fast it is cleared</span> · 1 published case</span>`, ''))}
   ${note('A team chooses in its settings whether it is listed, and what it says about itself here. Being listed changes nothing about what its members see or do.')}${note('The people who make Civicsmith decline or remove a listing only under a published listing rule, never for a team\'s views or for whom it holds to account. A team is always told why.')}<details class="mk-details"><summary>The listing rule</summary><p class="mk-small" style="margin:6px 0 0">civicsmith.org lists every team whose administrators choose to list it. We decline or remove a listing only when it (1) is not a team using Civicsmith, or is advertising or spam; (2) pretends to be another team, person or office; (3) publishes something a court has ordered removed, or that is unlawful to publish; or (4) aims at a private person rather than at a government's work: their home, family or private life. We never decline or remove a listing for a team's views, its conclusions, or whom it holds to account, public officials and companies included. We tell the team which part of this rule applies and why; once it is fixed, the team can ask again.</p></details></div>
  <div class="st st-d">${nav('c')}${h1('Teams at work', 'The teams that chose to be listed here, each with what it has published. A team may keep itself to its members; then it is not listed, and nothing on this page is asked of it.')}
   ${note('No team is listed yet. A team appears here once its administrators choose, in their own team\'s Civicsmith, to list it and what it has published.')}${note('The people who make Civicsmith decline or remove a listing only under a published listing rule, never for a team\'s views or for whom it holds to account. A team is always told why.')}<details class="mk-details"><summary>The listing rule</summary><p class="mk-small" style="margin:6px 0 0">civicsmith.org lists every team whose administrators choose to list it. We decline or remove a listing only when it (1) is not a team using Civicsmith, or is advertising or spam; (2) pretends to be another team, person or office; (3) publishes something a court has ordered removed, or that is unlawful to publish; or (4) aims at a private person rather than at a government's work: their home, family or private life. We never decline or remove a listing for a team's views, its conclusions, or whom it holds to account, public officials and companies included. We tell the team which part of this rule applies and why; once it is fixed, the team can ask again.</p></details></div>` }; };

/* DEC-430 (B513; installer R85): the questions people ask, one block, the same on every step. */
const INSTALL_QA = () => sec(`Questions people ask`, `<details class="mk-details"><summary>Why does my team need its own Cloudflare account?</summary><p class="mk-small" style="margin:6px 0 0">So that nobody else holds your team's work: the people who make Civicsmith keep none of it and can't open your account. Whoever can sign in to the account controls your team's Civicsmith, so use an account that belongs to your team, and add a second trusted person to it.</p></details>` + `<details class="mk-details"><summary>What does it cost, who is paid, and how do we stop paying?</summary><p class="mk-small" style="margin:6px 0 0">About $5 a month for Workers Paid, and R2 storage beyond the 10 GB Cloudflare includes, all paid to Cloudflare only. Nothing is paid to the people who make Civicsmith. To stop paying, cancel Workers Paid in Cloudflare's dashboard. Your team's Civicsmith stops working when the plan ends, so agree on it as a team first.</p></details>` + `<details class="mk-details"><summary>What can Civicsmith see and do in our account, and how do we remove it?</summary><p class="mk-small" style="margin:6px 0 0">The installer can create and update your team's Civicsmith's own programs and storage, and nothing else, and it keeps no access afterward. To remove your team's Civicsmith, use the installer's page, or delete its parts in Cloudflare's dashboard, in Workers &amp; Pages and in R2.</p></details>` + `<details class="mk-details"><summary>Is our card shared with Civicsmith?</summary><p class="mk-small" style="margin:6px 0 0">No. Your payment method stays with Cloudflare. The installer never sees it, and the permission you give can't reach billing.</p></details>` + `<details class="mk-details"><summary>What if we already use Cloudflare?</summary><p class="mk-small" style="margin:6px 0 0">Use that account if it belongs to your team: your team's Civicsmith is added beside what's already there under its own names, nothing else is changed, and the installer checks there is room. If the account is one person's, open a separate one for the team. If it already holds a Civicsmith, the installer says so and asks what you'd like to do.</p></details>` + `<details class="mk-details"><summary>What if we get stuck?</summary><p class="mk-small" style="margin:6px 0 0">Close the installer at any step and come back: it opens where you left off, and nothing is lost. Cloudflare's own help pages explain each of its steps, and when something is missing, the installer says exactly what.</p></details>`);
